	(text "Power-On Delay Circuit (High-Pass / Decay Topology)\n\nGoal: Disable buffer (~{OE} = High) during MCU boot (~3ms), then enable it.\n\nComponent Values:\n* C = 100 nF (Connected between +5V and Schmitt-trigger input)\n* R = 100 kΩ (Connected between Schmitt-trigger input and GND)\n\nTiming Calculations (Vcc = 5.0V):\n* Schmitt-Trigger Negative Threshold (Vt-) ≈ 2.5V (*** Worst case scenario at 5.5V)\n* Equation: t = -R * C * ln(Vt- / Vcc)\n* Calculation: t = -100kΩ * 100nF * ln(2.5V / 5.0V)\n* Calculation: t = -0.01 * ln(0.50) ≈ 6.93 ms\n\nResult:\nProvides a ~6.93 ms delay before enabling the buffer, leaving a safe ~3.93 ms\nmargin for the MCU to boot and stabilize its data outputs.\n\nhttps://www.lcsc.com/datasheet/C10429.pdf"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 90.678 120.65 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.15)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "58e1494c-5be5-4faf-9d19-68ce002a2ee7")
	)
	(text "*** NOTE: \nThis Schmitt buffer is not required here; \nhowever, the stock IC is a dual buffer IC, \nand so the spare gate is used for convenience."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 42.164 48.26 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "KiCad Font")
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "93016e3c-61e5-4d95-b351-8a7db07dbcd5")
	)
